        "completedSourceTexts": [
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-shanxi-taiyuan-2025-m1:grammar-fill:1",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-shanxi-taiyuan-2025-m1:grammar-fill:1",
            "text": "The winter holiday season shines with decorations and lights. It is this time of year when Harbin, known as the city of ice, becomes a winter wonderland wrapped in silver and white."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-shanxi-taiyuan-2025-m1:grammar-fill:2",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-shanxi-taiyuan-2025-m1:grammar-fill:2",
            "text": "In Harbin, what catches our eyes and leaves us stunned is its ice sculptures, which are more than frozen art, but a symbol of human wisdom, proving that even in the extreme cold, beauty can thrive."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-shanxi-taiyuan-2025-m1:grammar-fill:3",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-shanxi-taiyuan-2025-m1:grammar-fill:3",
            "text": "On the frozen Songhua River, the only source of crystal-clear and bubble-free ice, workers are busy harvesting thousands of cubic meters of ice to build the splendid Ice and Snow World. They slice the surface into blocks of the same size, each weighing 700 kg. At the construction site, to support massive structures like twin ice towers, engineers first build steel frames up to 40 meters tall, around which ice blocks are piled like bricks. Then they fill the gaps between frames and blocks with ice and water, which freeze instantly to rock-solid walls. For unique structures, workers apply water mixed with paper pulp (纸浆) onto a blown-up mould (模具), creating ice three times stronger than normal. Days later, the mould is removed, revealing an amazing, durable creation. LED lights are embedded in carved sinks, layer by layer, changing sculptures into glowing wonders."
          },
          {
            "textId": "done-block:paper-mock-shanxi-taiyuan-2025-m1:grammar-fill:4",
            "paragraphId": "block:paper-mock-shanxi-taiyuan-2025-m1:grammar-fill:4",
            "text": "Despite immense challenges – slippery surfaces, -25°Cand time limit, the teams work 24/7 in shifts. Their dedication turns raw ice into breathtaking art – the art itself is momentary, but the experience and the delicate beauty will last forever."
          }
        ],
